Feature: slice-3 / email-verification-gate
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-3
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 (the post-signup "we sent you" page).

What was built
==============
Extended `src/components/register/ResendVerificationButton.tsx`
(originally a single-shot resend button from feature 1) into a
full verify-email gate:

  1. Polls `auth.currentUser.reload()` every 5s while the user
     is signed in but unverified. Firebase's JS SDK doesn't push
     email-verified changes — reload() refreshes the ID token's
     emailVerified claim in place.
  2. Listens to `document.visibilitychange` so when the user
     clicks the email link in another tab and comes back to this
     one, the next reload() fires immediately instead of waiting
     up to 5s.
  3. On `user.emailVerified === true`:
       - sets status="verified"
       - shows a "✓ E-mail potwierdzony · Przekierowujemy do
         aplikacji…" panel with a manual "Przejdź do aplikacji"
         button (in case the auto-redirect's window.location is
         blocked).
       - 1.5s delay → window.location =
         https://app.superwizor.ai/login (cross-origin, per §5 R3).
  4. Resend button still available the whole time. Polite live
     region ("Sprawdzamy potwierdzenie…") visible when signed in
     and not yet verified.

Why a poll + visibilitychange and not a Firebase action handler?
- Firebase's "action link" flow lands the user on
  /__/auth/action?mode=verifyEmail&oobCode=… which is the
  Firebase-hosted page. The continueUrl can bring them back to a
  configured route; we use that for resilient back-nav. The poll
  here is the second leg of redundancy — if the user clicks the
  email link in their inbox app (Gmail, native Mail) the
  verification happens server-side and our page just notices on
  the next reload(). No custom action handler needed.

