How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table unchanged (only the verify-
   email page's client island was modified). 21 SSG + 2 dynamic +
   proxy.

2. HTTP smoke:
     /register/therapist/verify-email?email=anna@example.com    → 200
     /en/register/therapist/verify-email?email=anna@example.com → 200

3. Puppeteer screenshots:
   - verify-email-pl-full.png — Polish, fullPage. Shows the
     "Sprawdź swoją skrzynkę" + email interpolation +
     "WYŚLIJ PONOWNIE" + "Powrót do strony głównej". The
     "Sprawdzamy potwierdzenie…" status is gated on a signed-in
     user (auth.currentUser !== null); puppeteer hits the page
     without an active sign-in so it's correctly hidden in the
     screenshot. The polling code path activates only when a
     real user is signed in.
   - verify-email-en-full.png — same composition in English.
   - verify-email-pl-{mobile,tablet,desktop}.png — viewport-
     clipped responsiveness.

4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs". The
   reload() call would throw on a stale token; the try/catch in
   the poll function swallows it and just retries on the next
   interval.

How the verified UI was confirmed (without a real Firebase user)
================================================================
Live emailVerified=true cannot be triggered in this session
without:
  - A real Firebase project + Auth emulator running, OR
  - Hand-modifying auth-provider.tsx to inject a mock user.
Neither is in scope for an infrastructure-only smoke. Feature 8
(registration-e2e-playwright) covers the live happy path:
puppeteer signs up via the real form → emulator's
admin-confirm-email API marks the user verified → poll detects
the change → redirect fires. That's the genuine E2E test for
this gate.

What's intentionally NOT wired here
===================================
- A route-level "unverified visitor → bounce back to
  verify-email" middleware. There's no protected page on the
  marketing site yet (everything is public) so the gate is
  purely UI-level. When Slice 5's Flutter Web app comes online,
  its router will check `auth.currentUser.emailVerified` on
  protected routes — separate concern from this Slice 3 feature.

